<title>AUSTRALIA: Diamond Rose shares sparkle on debut.</title>
<headline>Diamond Rose shares sparkle on debut.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in gemstone explorer Diamond Rose NL made their debut on the Australian Stock Exchange at A$1.508, a spectacular premium of A$1.308 on their issue price of 20 cents.</p>
<p>Fifty million shares were issued, raising A$10 million.</p>
<p>The company's major assets are tenements from an unlisted company associated with director Pnina Feldman, a sister of mining tycoon Joseph Gutnick.</p>
<p>By 11.45 a.m. (0145 GMT), Diamond Rose shares were at A$1.35 after reaching a high of A$1.75 and a low of A$1.10.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
